// =========================================================================
// FILE: stdlib/core/syntax/exits.pilot
// HOW A FUNCTION IS LEFT: `errdefer` AND `become`
// =========================================================================
// `errdefer stmt` / `errdefer { .. }` is a `defer` that runs only when its
// block is left by a failure: a `?` that propagates, or a `return` of a
// value `?` would propagate. Leaving any other way skips it. It runs
// last-in, first-out together with the block's `defer`s. It is a `defer`
// node whose flags are 1.
//
// `become f(args);` is a guaranteed tail call: `f` takes over the caller's
// frame and its value is the caller's value, so a chain of any length runs
// in constant stack. The callee must return the caller's type (TAIL003),
// it must be a call (TAIL001), and no `defer` or `errdefer` may still be
// waiting to run (TAIL002). It is a `return` node whose flags are 1.
// =========================================================================
[EnforceCoreNaming]
pub lvl(Cfg.Tokens.ring_genesis) pkg Pilot.Core.Syntax.Exits;

use Pilot.Core.Genesis.*;

comptime {
    __engine("bind_receptor", nameof(errdefer), 38, 0);
    __engine("bind_receptor", nameof(become),   39, 0);
}
